[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) says one issue, one fix queued. Its reports say otherwise: they describe
three problems, and the queued parser fix closes one of them.

<Callout kind="warn">
#4471 is not one bug. Fixing the parser leaves the booking-v3 date hint and the one-day shift open.
</Callout>

## The split

<SplitTable ticket={4471} {tickets} />

## What each problem is

- **`parser`**: the shared parser reads every date month first. Every tenant on file writes the day
  first, so any date with a day up to 12 comes out with day and month swapped. This is the bug
  #4471 is named for.
- **`hint`**: the booking-v3 form prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field. People type month
  first because the form tells them to, and the form reads the date the tenant's way, day first. It
  happens only through the form, only at booking-v3 tenants. The parser fix does not touch it; the
  hint or the form's read order must change.
- **`shift`**: the date moves by one day, not a day/month swap. The same meeting shows Tuesday in
  Lisbon and Monday in Toronto; an invite arrives before the booking. This reads as timezone
  handling. The desk noted these reports (`desk-notes.json`) but filed them under `parser` by
  tenant, so they had no ticket.

## How the reports were counted

- The export repeats some rows where its pages overlap: one id, one report.
- Each report is placed by its tenant's locale and booking form and its channel
  (`#lib/kb/causes.ts`), not by intake's tag. Intake tags follow the reporter's browser and
  disagree with the cause on both sides.
- Reports the desk read as a one-day move get their own cause (`#lib/kb/split.ts`).
- Every number on this page is computed from `reports-4471.json` at render time.

## Why they ended up in one ticket

[Decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) merges on subject line alone. All three
problems arrive under the same subjects ("Wrong day on the invite", "Dates mixed up"), so subject
matching cannot keep them apart. Split by cause, as the [triage explorer](/kb/triage/dedupe)
already does, before marking a big ticket known.

